<title>JAPAN: Cabin surges on restructuring plan.</title>
<headline>Cabin surges on restructuring plan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Cabin Co Ltd surged on Wednesday morning on the company's restructuring plan, brokers said.</p>
<p>The shares finished the morning session at 330 yen, up 22 yen from the previous day's close. They ranked fourth in the list of top percentage gainers on the Tokyo Stock Exchange's first section.</p>
<p>The women's wear retailer said on Tuesday it would close about 70 shops in the next year which it believed unlikely to return to profit.</p>
<p>It currently has a total of 396 shops, all in Japan.</p>
</text>
